      "body": "## Motivation\n\nLazy Mamba buffers contain unused entries marked `-1`. Closing or aborting a streaming session returned these entries to the pool, so 8 slots could become 9 free slots, including an invalid one.\n\nRelated #39838. The report's private 8-GPU workload has not been reproduced.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSkip unused entries when counting and releasing session buffers. Rebased on current main and updated the regression tests to use the current request release path.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n22 related CPU tests and 8 subtests pass. On current main without the fix, all 4 lazy-buffer regression cases fail with `9 != 8`; regular buffers pass.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable to this buffer cleanup change; model calculations are unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changed-file pre-commit checks pass.\n- [x] Regression tests fail before the fix and pass after it.\n- [x] SGLang code style followed.\n- Documentation changes are not needed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36281197970](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36281197970)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36281197906](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36281197906)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36281198004](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36281198004)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
